   "depends_on": [
    "#36369"
   ],
   "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "This PR is stacked on top of open PR #36369. Nine of the ten commits and all consensus/P2P/validation diffs belong to #36369; only the final commit adding `src/test/fuzz/p2p_1p1c_liveness.cpp` (+402 lines) is unique to this pull request.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Diff is now available; the PR remains stacked on #36369 with no changes to the proposed fuzzing harness approach.",
  "card": "Adds the p2p_1p1c_liveness fuzz target to test end-to-end 1p1c package relay liveness using live PeerManager, P2P message processing, and validation components. Existing download manager harnesses model validation results rather than invoking validation directly, leaving blind spots where adversarial peers delivering malleated transactions or triggering specific validation failures could disrupt package resolution from honest peers. The harness asserts that acceptable packages announced by honest peers always enter the mempool despite adversary stalls, malleation, or disconnections. Stacked on #36369, which provides the underlying fixes and base test updates.",
